## 🎨 Part 5: Restoring Theme Styling, Fonts, & Colors

We extracted the original site's style tags and custom settings. Recreating your fonts, headings, layout structure, and audio player design is as simple as adding a single block of code to your new WordPress site.

### Extracted Theme Config:
* **Headers Font**: `Lobster` (size `36px` for `h1`)
* **Body/Paragraphs Font**: `Overlock`
* **Vibrant Accent Color**: `#26ade5` (Vibrant Blue, used for links hover and active states)
* **Background Color**: `#f9f8f8` (Soft Off-white)
* **Background Pattern**: The site used a subtle `noisy_grid.png` background repetition.

### How to apply this CSS block:
1. Log in to your WordPress dashboard.
2. Go to **Appearance > Customize** (or **Appearance > Additional CSS** depending on your active theme).
3. Open the **Additional CSS** tab.
4. Copy and paste the entire block below into the editor box, then hit **Publish**. It will automatically load the correct Google Fonts and style your site to match the original.

```css
/* 
==================================================================
  PETER N GHENT - WEBSITE RESTORATION CUSTOM CSS
  Copy and paste this entire block into:
  Appearance > Customize > Additional CSS in your WordPress Dashboard
================================================================== 
*/

/* 1. IMPORT GOOGLE FONTS */
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Open+Sans:ital,wght@0,300;0,400;0,600;1,300;1,400;1,600&family=Overlock&family=Lobster&display=swap');

/* 2. BASE TYPOGRAPHY & COLORS */
body {
    font-family: 'Overlock', sans-serif;
    color: #6a6767;
    background-color: #f9f8f8;
}

p {
    font-family: 'Overlock', sans-serif;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
}

h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
    font-family: 'Lobster', cursive;
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 400;
}

h1 {
    font-size: 36px;
}

/* Links & Accents */
a, p a, span a, h1 a, h2 a, h3 a, h4 a, h5 a, h6 a {
    color: #333333;
    transition: color 0.2s ease-in-out;
}

a:hover, p a:hover, span a:hover, h1 a:hover, h2 a:hover, h3 a:hover, h4 a:hover, h5 a:hover, h6 a:hover {
    color: #26ade5; /* Vibrant Blue Accent */
}

/* 3. HOME PAGE LAYOUT OVERRIDES */
.home .site-content {
    width: 100%;
}

/* 4. CUSTOM GRID COLUMNS (ROW1 & COLUMN) */
.row1 {
    width: 100%;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
}

.column {
    float: left;
    width: 25%;
    text-align: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: 10px;
}

/* Clear floats after the columns */
.row1:after {
    content: "";
    display: table;
    clear: both;
}

@media screen and (max-width: 767px) {
    .column {
        width: 100%;
    }
}

/* 5. AUDIO ALBUM PLUGIN CUSTOM COLORS */
/* Set clean Verdana font for Audio elements */
.audioheading,
.audioalbum,
.track {
    font-family: 'Verdana', sans-serif !important;
}

/* Dark grey/slate player theme */
.audioalbum, 
.audioheading, 
.track {
    background-color: #434a54 !important;
}

/* Inner controls bar and download/audio buttons */
.track .wp-audio-shortcode.mejs-audio .mejs-inner > .mejs-controls,
.track .audiobutton a {
    background-color: #2c3138 !important;
}

.track .audiobutton a:hover {
    background-color: #ffffff !important;
    color: #434a54 !important;
}

/* White track timeline slider progress */
.track .mejs-time-rail .mejs-time-total .mejs-time-current,
.track .mejs-controls .mejs-horizontal-volume-slider .mejs-horizontal-volume-current {
    background-color: #ffffff !important;
}

/* Darker timeline background and volume bars */
.track .mejs-controls .mejs-time-rail .mejs-time-total,
.track .mejs-time-rail .mejs-time-total .mejs-time-loaded,
.track .mejs-controls .mejs-horizontal-volume-slider .mejs-horizontal-volume-total {
    background-color: #2c3138 !important;
}

/* White text for song info and details */
h1.audioheading,
p.audioheading,
h2.audioalbum,
p.audioalbum,
.track .songtitle,
.track .songwriter,
.track .mejs-controls > .mejs-button button,
.track .audiobutton a,
.track .mejs-currenttime,
.track .mejs-duration {
    color: #ffffff !important;
}

.track .mejs-controls > .mejs-button button:hover {
    color: #ffffff !important;
}
```

